  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $y=2\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(1+x)$ at $x=-1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(1+x)] \\\\  & =2(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(1+x)^{2}}})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1+x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-(1+2x+{x}^{2})}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{-2x-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve at $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{-2(-1)-(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
